WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.211 --> 00:00:17.152
heart pounded.

2
00:00:17.172 --> 00:00:19.773
"Please don't send Sunny away, Jon!

3
00:00:20.814 --> 00:00:24.216
He ran off, but he felt me slipping—and stopped right away!"

4
00:00:24.236 --> 00:00:28.698
"That's good to hear," Jan said.

5
00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:33.469
"Yes, but Jon shook his head.

6
00:00:33.489 --> 00:00:37.271
"We have enough to do without a green horse to train."

7
00:00:50.438 --> 00:00:51.619
Daisy dismounted.

8
00:00:51.639 --> 00:00:55.401
"Sunny also found his way back to the farm.

9
00:00:55.941 --> 00:00:57.062
He knows it's his home!"

10
00:00:57.882 --> 00:01:00.724
"He's a great horse," Jan said sadly.

11
00:01:01.388 --> 00:01:02.469
"But Jon's right.

12
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:10.652
If an experienced young rider can't control him on the trail, he's too green.

13
00:01:11.272 --> 00:01:12.473
We can't keep him."

14
00:01:12.493 --> 00:01:16.074
"I have to tell you something."

15
00:01:16.654 --> 00:01:18.235
Daisy took a deep breath.

16
00:01:18.255 --> 00:01:21.236
"I'm not an experienced rider.

17
00:01:21.696 --> 00:01:23.737
I lied because I wanted to ride Sunny."

18
00:01:23.757 --> 00:01:27.119
"What?" Jan looked shocked.

19
00:01:27.139 --> 00:01:31.933
"During the lesson I was so focused on Grace, I didn't even notice!"

20
00:01:31.953 --> 00:01:33.655
"I'm sorry."

21
00:01:34.155 --> 00:01:35.636
Daisy felt miserable.

22
00:01:35.656 --> 00:01:37.878
"But please don't send Sunny back.

23
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.061
It's my fault he ran away."

24
00:01:41.922 --> 00:01:44.123
Jon and Jan stared at each other.

25
00:01:45.385 --> 00:01:46.786
Daisy was near tears.

26
00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:50.028
"I wanted to help Sunny," she thought.

27
00:01:50.048 --> 00:01:53.231
"Instead I made things worse—way worse!"

28
00:01:54.332 --> 00:01:58.035
Squeal! Just then a pig charged into the barn.

29
00:02:02.256 --> 00:02:04.117
"Hubert! He escaped again!"

30
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:05.317
Kaleem yelled.

31
00:02:07.438 --> 00:02:09.118
Blossom whinnied and backed up.

32
00:02:09.978 --> 00:02:12.559
Ozzy spun in a circle, looking terrified.

33
00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:14.960
Grace looked terrified too.

34
00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.461
But Sunny immediately pricked his ears.

35
00:02:18.481 --> 00:02:20.101
"It's the pig!"

36
00:02:20.461 --> 00:02:21.401
he said happily.

37
00:02:22.282 --> 00:02:24.462
Daisy suddenly got an idea.

38
00:02:24.482 --> 00:02:30.144
"The other horses are terrified, Sunny," she whispered.

39
00:02:30.988 --> 00:02:32.829
"We have to get Hubert out of here."

40
00:02:34.249 --> 00:02:34.989
"No problem!"

41
00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.770
Daisy led the horse toward Hubert.

42
00:02:43.012 --> 00:02:44.152
back, pig!"

43
00:02:44.212 --> 00:02:44.872
Sunny said.

44
00:02:51.094 --> 00:02:55.176
Hubert squealed loudly as Daisy kept her hand on Sunny's reins.

45
00:02:59.136 --> 00:03:01.817
Then together they backed Hubert out the doors!

46
00:03:01.837 --> 00:03:05.118
"I've got him now!"

47
00:03:05.398 --> 00:03:08.499
Kaleem said, chasing Hubert back into the pigpen.

48
00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:13.260
Ozzy and Blossom quickly settled down.

49
00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.001
"Good thinking, Daisy!"

50
00:03:16.381 --> 00:03:17.041
Jan said.

51
00:03:17.061 --> 00:03:21.982
"And great horse handling—Sunny stayed so calm."

52
00:03:25.303 --> 00:03:26.223
Daisy grinned.

53
00:03:26.243 --> 00:03:28.584
"I told you, he's a great horse!"

54
00:03:29.908 --> 00:03:30.729
Jon nodded.

55
00:03:30.749 --> 00:03:33.691
"But he's still green, and we're so busy.

56
00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:38.054
I don't think—" "What if we helped out?"

57
00:03:39.215 --> 00:03:41.496
Daisy looked at Kaleem and Grace, who nodded.

58
00:03:41.516 --> 00:03:44.518
"School will be out soon, so we can come often."

59
00:03:44.538 --> 00:03:48.861
"I can help with other stuff around the farm too," Kaleem said.

60
00:03:49.742 --> 00:03:51.903
Jan and Jon stared at each other again.

61
00:03:52.884 --> 00:03:54.145
Daisy held her breath.

62
00:03:54.165 --> 00:03:56.587
"Please say yes," she thought.

63
00:03:56.607 --> 00:04:00.100
"Please." "What do you think?"

64
00:04:00.521 --> 00:04:01.721
Jan asked softly.

65
00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.282
"I think Jon said.

66
00:04:04.302 --> 00:04:08.484
"A green horse who stays calm under pressure is worth training."

67
00:04:09.705 --> 00:04:10.665
The kids cheered.

68
00:04:14.046 --> 00:04:17.348
As soon as everyone moved away, Daisy hugged Sunny.

69
00:04:17.368 --> 00:04:20.309
"I'm sorry I almost ruined things for you."

70
00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:22.930
"No problem," Sunny said.

71
00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.231
"We had a great trail ride together!"

72
00:04:25.851 --> 00:04:26.692
Daisy nodded.

73
00:04:27.816 --> 00:04:30.138
"Yes, but if I hadn't—" "Daisy?"

74
00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:31.960
Daisy spun around.

75
00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:35.142
Grace stood there with a confused expression.

76
00:04:35.162 --> 00:04:37.284
"Were you just.

77
00:04:37.304 --> 00:04:40.166
"Yes! I can talk to animals!"

78
00:04:40.506 --> 00:04:41.567
Daisy blurted out.

79
00:04:41.587 --> 00:04:46.972
"It sounds crazy, and I can tell you more, but—" "I knew it!"

80
00:04:47.412 --> 00:04:48.933
Grace said, smiling.

81
00:04:48.953 --> 00:04:52.716
"That's why you're so good with animals, isn't it?"

82
00:04:54.278 --> 00:04:55.459
Bzzz. Bzzz.

83
00:04:56.299 --> 00:04:56.820
"Oh no!"

84
00:04:57.132 --> 00:04:57.874
Daisy thought.

85
00:04:58.455 --> 00:05:00.299
Beatrice was hovering behind her!

86
00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:04.467
Had the bee just heard Daisy tell Grace her secret?
